"tipone":"1- Meet and communicate with local residents while on the move.\n",
"tiptwo":"2- Beware of pickpocketing,Since there are fewer eyes on your stuff, opportunistic thieves can quickly get away with your valuables after picking them up. Invest in an anti-theft backpack, to keep your gear safe, put your money and phone in your front pockets, and don't carry all your cash when you go out.\n",
"tipthree":"3- Play it safe by printing out multiple copies of your travel documents.Carry a few copies of your passport photos and other travel documents. You may need it in the most unexpected places to prove your credentials. It is always a good idea to keep pictures of important documents on your mobile phone.\n",
"tipfour":"4- Carry cash with you, but only as much as you need for the day.When going to any exotic country, it's easy to want to keep all your cash on hand, but in order to protect yourself from pickpockets (or even want to spend all your money in one day), carry as much as you need.\n",
"tipfive":"5- Pay attention to charging your phone at public charging stations. If you're out all day and your phone needs to be charged, public transit stations are great, but you have to be careful about the wires they use at those stations. Use only the charging cable, not the data cable. Data cables can put your personal information at risk depending on where it is used.\n",


